/tmp/real-ralph-state.json
*.log

# Secrets — .env is the per-host config (vLLM endpoint + key). Never commit.
#
# THE GLOB, NOT JUST THE NAME. A second run root wanted a second env, so .env.fresh was
# created beside it: a byte-for-byte copy of the key, untracked, in a PUBLIC repository, one
# git add -A away from being published. It also made every deploy stamp read -dirty, because
# the stamp counts untracked files, which is how it was noticed at all.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
attempt_3/verify/baseline/
attempt_4/results/
attempt_4/iter-001_failed_experiments/
attempt_4/mine_j8_to_j11.py
attempt_5/Dockerfile.j21-fitness
attempt_3/verify/baseline_summary.json

# attempt_7: ephemeral per-stage Qwen synthesis cache
/attempt_7/per_stage/
/attempt_7/telemetry/
target/

# timestamped backups (never commit)
*.bak.*
# observability outputs (regenerated per run)
attempt_*/telemetry/
HANDOFF.md

